        "note": "4 rows: PM10/PM2.5 for polProcessID 10710 over the four fuel types, model years 1940-2060, and the ratio is 6.6667 on ALL FOUR. So unlike process-brakewear's eight-row table -- two model-year ranges carrying three distinct values -- this one cannot tell a correct lookup from one that dropped the range predicate and the fuel key. J36 carries both anyway, because the join is the port and this snapshot is one point of its input space; docs/process-tirewear.md 7.2 records which half of it is checked here and which by process-brakewear.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
